\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The stepwise gauge ledger and source-locked scope matrix. ``Certified'' means that the stated formula or algebraicity consequence is justified under the row's assumptions; ``stop/out'' means that the action certificate cannot be applied; ``edge'' marks a logarithm-domain exception or a statement needing separate interpretation. The cell provenance is recorded separately as frozen-JSON-derived or theorem-defined; the latter is not presented as a raw computational result. In particular, an algebraic endpoint mismatch retains the prime-log exclusion, while $\qopname  \relax o{log}|\mathcal  A|$ remains outside the theorem.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gauge-scope}{{2}{6}{The stepwise gauge ledger and source-locked scope matrix. ``Certified'' means that the stated formula or algebraicity consequence is justified under the row's assumptions; ``stop/out'' means that the action certificate cannot be applied; ``edge'' marks a logarithm-domain exception or a statement needing separate interpretation. The cell provenance is recorded separately as frozen-JSON-derived or theorem-defined; the latter is not presented as a raw computational result. In particular, an algebraic endpoint mismatch retains the prime-log exclusion, while $\log |\Action |$ remains outside the theorem}{figure.2}{}}
